# rm470, the chair on the skids (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm470
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_rue_haycombe
written_by codex
title the chair on the skids
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=farmer
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk slides_a_facing_chair_to_the_orchard_door
likes hard_cheese singing old_maps summer_evenings
dislikes waiting salt_wind
fears overlooking_a_caller_with_both_arms_full
hopes for_a_returning_voice_to_find_a_place_at_supper
topics work +0.6 home +0.4 pastimes +0.3 weather +0.2
styles comfort=warm gossip=plain refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps a chair on runners facing the orchard door, ready to slide out and take a caller's load.

words
oath! = My crooked chair skids | Bless the back orchard gate
saying! = Slide over and take an end | Good shoulders earn their supper
skids = my oak chair runners | the two polished skids
crate = a slatted fruit box | an empty harvest crate
rind = a sharp cheese wedge | some sharp hard cheese
song = the long picking song | the last harvest verse
door = the loading door | my broad orchard doorway
hock = the back chair leg | the short rear leg
map = a crooked road map | a map with a forgotten turning
handle = the worn hand slot | the smooth lifting grip
letter = a folded scrap | a small square of writing paper
burr = a latching burr | a seed caught in the ruff
gust = the salt draught | a draught tasting of brine
light = long summer light | the last yellow light

any
opinion @1 dole for 2 : An orchard table doesn't grow poorer for cutting a wedge for a hungry wolf.
opinion @1 festivals against 1 : I want a tune giving me a chance to hear who came in halfway. A street full of shouting spoils the verse.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Fresh shoulders can help lift the day as readily as a familiar pair.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : A road greeting ought to get a wolf as far as the cheese plate.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I've followed the homeward smell of spent apple leaves for too many years to want another city.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Slide your load this way. Welcome. | I can see you fine from this seat.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes] : Come clear of that crate lip. | Welcome, there's an end free to lean on.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The apples are still cool. | Good light on the orchard door.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Bring that chair into earshot. | Welcome under the last picking light.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Household voices deserve first cut of cheese. | Bring your face into the good light.
line @1 again.open : Found the runners again, I see. | We can take that other end now.
line @1 greet.return : Good to see your shoulders clear the door. | Back within reach of a cheese wedge.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You've a welcome warm enough to sing in. | Slide over, familiar face.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I'll put my box down for company. | Good to see where the help is coming from.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : I left the lamp facing outwards. | Come catch the last of our light.
line @1 farewell : Keep a steady hold downhill. | May your load reach the right door.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll look up for you next time. | Come back with a verse to spare.
line @2 farewell.return [here.time=night] : Mind the soft verge on your way home. | Some light hangs above the leaf line.
line @1 react.news : Set down the load and let me hear. | Pass me the plain account.
line @1 react.news.new : That landed fresh in my lap. | New as this season's first windfall.
line @1 react.news.known : I've had my shoulders under that story before. | That one came up the orchard road earlier.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd look for another witness before hauling that any farther. | Somebody's added a weight that never grew on that tree.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll take an end if the weight gets too much. | A bitter thing to have fetched home.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : I'd put a verse to such good fortune. | That's worth a generous second cutting.
line @1 ask.how : How's the load sitting today? | What weight have you carried in here?
line @1 answer.how : A fair load, and a chair that answers. | I've a thorn in my patience. Otherwise sound.
line @1 decline : I'll have to keep my shoulders for the evening crates. | A wolf with free paws would serve you better.
line @1 accept_decline : Set it down then. I've heard you. | Let the empty box stay empty.
line @1 thank : You saw the weight and pitched in. | I felt that kindness at my end.
line @1 sympathise : Turn your chair towards this bit of light. | Have some sharp cheese while your voice comes back.
line @1 reassure : We can start with one small box between us. | There's room to take a second hold.
line @1 preclose : My facing chair is wanted at the door. | That last row can't bring itself indoors.
scene skids
when topic=work self.job=farmer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put #skids# under a chair so I could turn it to face #door# without lifting it.
b : Why bother with runners? | Is it a good working seat?
a : I'd see the next caller coming. Some come in with a crate high enough to cover a face. | Fine. I can slide it well away before a heavy load comes through.

scene box
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My fingers look for #handle# before the lifting starts.
b : A loose slat? | What about a sharp edge?
a : One bad grip breaks more fruit than the journey down from the tree. | I rub it smooth. Somebody else may get the same box full.

scene cheese
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll give #rind# to a visitor before asking for the news.
b : Even at a busy hour? | How much do you cut?
a : A busy hour can be a hungry one. That's my reasoning. | A broad enough wedge to let a guest breathe before speaking.

scene verse
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sing #song# in a key that suits a load going uphill.
b : Low or high? | Do you change it downhill?
a : Low. Save the breath for lifting and let the leaves take the finer notes. | Coming down with an empty crate I can make quite a different noise.

scene map
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me #map# to see a road running clean through an old tree.
b : Is the road wrong? | Do you mark the tree?
a : The tree certainly hasn't stirred out of stubbornness. The drawer ought to have come here in person. | With a seed if I have one. I won't spoil an entertaining mistake in ink.

scene wait
when topic=work self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A cart dawdling while I stand beside an empty stool makes me considerably crosser than an ordinary late delivery.
b : Could you sit down? | Why stay there?
a : Once I've dragged the stool round to face the track. I can't settle with the road at my back. | Somebody must take the first crate. I'm considerably pleasanter once there's lifting to do.

scene wind
when topic=weather self.dislikes=salt_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I lift my ruff against #gust# and get a whole harvest of burrs down my neck.
b : Worth stopping for? | How do they get there?
a : The big ones yes. I can't sing with a seed trying to play accompaniment against my ear. | I get under low boughs for the best fruit. There are costs to being thorough.

scene longlight
when topic=weather self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In #light# I can see which apples keep a last fleck of sun on the skin.
b : Do you pick those? | Does that fleck affect the flavour?
a : By the time I've admired one it's usually grown too dark to choose its neighbours. It gets left for morning. | I can see a difference. I'll leave tasting as a separate pleasure.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like to hear #self.friend# join me for a verse out beyond the rows.
b : Where do you start? | Would you take food?
a : Any note that comes easily through a tired throat. This isn't a temple choir. | Hard cheese and an apple cut through the middle. Nothing that calls for a second journey.

scene silence
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sometimes I lay #letter# beside my plate and can't think how to begin it.
b : Do you expect a reply? | What do you finally put?
a : A long road may carry my news one way even if the road back has gone quiet. | Which tree came into flower first. A wolf far away might still remember it.

scene guest
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two steps in from the loading door is a fine safe place where a newcomer can wait.
b : How can a stranger tell? | Out of the traffic?
a : I take the first crate and show the spot with my heel. There's no need to guess under a full load. | Clear of the swing and within reach of the cheese. Both count.

scene merit
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A box of sound fruit is easier to price when somebody remembers who carried it in.
b : You count the shoulders? | Does a bruise lower the price?
a : And the wood and the waiting. A tree does very little hauling by itself. | Of course. It doesn't take the soundness out of every other apple in the box.

scene open
when topic=home self.street
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like my first step home on #self.street# to come after I've heard the load settle properly.
b : Can you hear that much? | Do you miss the orchard indoors?
a : Wood quits complaining a little before fruit does. That second quiet sends me home. | At times. I don't miss watching for wheels while I cut my supper.

scene faith
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For one moment under full blossom I can hold my peace quite naturally.
b : Just one moment? | What do you ask then?
a : Listening under blossoms takes less effort than standing quietly inside a doorway for an hour. | For enough full branches that nobody comes away with a basket of excuses.

scene doors
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Sit in the comfortable seat if you'll leave me the one facing the entrance.
b : Bad back? | Afraid of visitors?
a : Perfectly good back. I watch for callers needing a hand before a load is dropped. | It's company I want. I prefer to get a welcome in first.

scene gather
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A festival crowd could do with the order of an orchard picking song.
b : Would you lead it? | How does it help?
a : Only within reach of a sensible exit. I don't much like voices all knocking together. | A verse to lift and a verse to set down. There's space in between for the next wolf.

scene sharp
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I get sharp enough for cheese rind when a crate's left across a doorway.
b : Do you move it? | What do you say?
a : First move it, then speak. By then I usually have enough breath to say something civil. | Exactly where I'd like it carried. There's small sense in making a sermon out of a box.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed a whole orchard could roll indoors on my chair runners when the weather turned.
b : Room for all the trees? | What woke you?
a : Not even one. I was trying to argue a bough through my front door and neither of us would give. | A branch tapping the roof. I was glad of one last tree with decent outdoor habits.

story runner [topic=memories]
  : My old chair caught the same floor crack every morning. One day the seat arrived at the loading door a good pace ahead of its hind legs.
  : I found two lengths of smooth oak instead of hunting for a better crack. Now the legs travel in company and my visitors get to see my face.
  b : Did you fill the crack afterwards?
  : I laid the chair across it first and had a good long sit. Some repairs deserve to see the trouble from above.

story rindroad [topic=pastimes]
  : A crumb of cheese on an old map once looked remarkably like a farmhouse at a bend I'd forgotten. I spent a whole supper remembering its window.
  : Then I brushed the crumb away. The farmhouse had never been on the page. I'd put it back out of my own head while looking at that scrap of rind.
  b : Was it sad to lose it again?
  : I carry that window with me still. I value the map for knowing when to let go.

story loadsong [topic=work self.job=farmer]
  : I tried using a particularly fine high tune to put heart into the last uphill haul. I reached my top note just as my crate slipped.
  : I set the load safely down and sang that note sitting beside it. Afterwards I carried the apples home to three plain low notes and no clever turns.
  b : Do you still use the fine tune?
  : In my chair after supper. A voice ought to have a good night out too.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.working=yes self.job=farmer
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Slats straight, paws beneath the hand slots. | Make a clear way for a full fruit box.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=hard_cheese
does aside
cooldown 7h
say A broad wedge for a long walk. | The rind belongs with the sharp bit.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark self.likes=old_maps
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A tree parting the cart ruts in two. | That crooked bend found a home on paper.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Runners round towards the fading light. | One last verse before the crates go quiet.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Slide my chair towards the door as you come through. I've a sharp cheese wedge and enough patience for plain speaking.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=farmer self.workplace] : The crates at #self.workplace# get their first rest after a long morning in the branches.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : Here's what's reached the orchard door. #world.news#
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I know that step. There's a fresh cutting of cheese within reach.
dlg @1 resident.bye : A smooth runner under whatever you carry home.
graft resident.hub
choice Why does the orchard chair run on skids? -> orchard_seat
node orchard_seat
say Take a short leg, give it a stubborn floor crack and see how far it'll follow the rest of the chair. My two oak runners take them all to the door together.
free
choice Why face the door in particular? -> orchard_load
choice I hope the chair holds up. -> hub
node orchard_load
say A falling crate needs another pair of shoulders. I can take an end from a stranger much more readily when I see it rocking towards me.
choice I'd take the lighter end to start. -> hub
choice Good luck with the picking. -> bye
